Momentum movement rewrite: slopes, wall-runs, vaults, dash, live tuning

Replace the precision controller (sprint button, charged jump, seven jump
kinds) with a momentum-based one where every move feeds speed into the next:

- Ground speed along the surface; speed builds the longer you run
- Ramps (steep and gentle) in the level format, editor and renderer;
  downhill speeds you up, ramp lips launch you
- Landings keep speed; jumping on landing gives a perfect-landing boost
- Slides gain speed downhill and carry into long jumps or a run
- Fast wall hits become wall-runs; low steps are vaulted; ledges mantled
- Air dash keeps existing momentum and refills on the ground
- Camera looks ahead and zooms out with speed; speed lines
- All values in assets/tuning.txt, hot-reloaded while playing
- F1 debug overlay with a speed graph; --debug and --screenshot flags
- Movement gym level teaching each move

